  "observations": [
    "Large live cohort per lifecycle: proof polls 64.7 (60.0 pending) before, 27.7 (23.3) with poll backoff only and 13.2 (11.2) after; per committed MiB 36.8 before and 7.5 after.",
    "Large live cohort: proof submissions per lifecycle 4.0 before and with poll backoff only, 2.0 after (resume and stop receipt); server proofs 12 to 6, server compute 10.7 s to 4.4 s per cohort, local prefix hashing 673 to 404 MiB per lifecycle.",
    "Resume was unchanged (2,083 ms before, 2,067 ms after). Three sequential stop receipts took 2,839 ms before, 3,328 ms with poll backoff only and 4,051 ms after: about 0.16 s more per receipt from coarser polling and 0.24 s more with the periodic change, consistent with receipts no longer reusing a just-completed periodic proof (before: 14 verified lookups for 12 submissions; after: 6 for 6). Each receipt stays within one second of its base time.",
    "Large live followers made 37.7 appends per lifecycle after against 62.3 before for the same committed bytes: periodic sweeps no longer add source checks between their pages, leaving the nominal one-second source-check cadence.",
    "Small live, quiet and mixed cohorts (prefixes up to 16 MiB) are unchanged within run-to-run variation; every disturbance still produced exactly one verification_unknown per follower with one recovery.",
    "All receipts verified, no transient retries, no dropped telemetry events."
  ],
  "dispositions": {
    "pendingProofPolls": "Adopted: bounded pending-poll backoff. With unchanged submissions the large cohort made 57% fewer polls (61% fewer pending); resume was unchanged and each finite receipt was delayed by less than one interval.",
    "periodicFullPrefixProofs": "Adopted: periodic interval scaled with prefix size above 16 MiB, at most 60 s. The large cohort halved its submissions, server compute fell 58% and local hashing 40%; small prefixes are unchanged.",
    "reusedProofLookups": "Superseded by task 45047152 (quietProofSkip below): under the A01M39QPB23CYS9QHCWQSATSJE9 amendment an unchanged periodic sweep completes locally while its verified result is under five minutes old and the latest heartbeat reports the same boundary; older results are never looked up and a fresh operation is submitted.",
    "appendsHeartbeatsMetadata": "No change to source-check, append, heartbeat or metadata logic.",
    "missRecovery": "Unchanged: bounded at four consecutive losses; one extra submission and one local rehash per loss."
  },
  "limitations": [
    "One host and loopback HTTP; no network shaping, packet loss or multi-host routing.",
    "Two runs per variant and one poll-backoff-only attribution run; stop timing aggregates three sequential receipts.",
    "Thirty-second live cohorts end before a 100 MiB follower reaches its 60 s periodic interval, so the measured periodic reduction is the removal of all in-window periodic sweeps; longer followers keep one sweep per minute.",
    "Restart is modelled by routing to a second server application with an empty registry sharing the database, not by restarting the native server.",
    "Server compute uses the registry clock from admission to the terminal result and includes queueing behind the two workers."
  ],
