      "Quiet cohorts: proof polls per lifecycle fell from 7.0-7.3 to 3.2-3.8 at unchanged submissions (2.0), heartbeats (6.0), server proofs and local hashing (8 MiB).",
      "Every disturbance still produced exactly one verification_unknown per follower with the expected reason (unknown_since_start, expired, evicted) and one recovery; with no periodic lookups the loss now surfaces at the stop-receipt lookup.",
      "Three sequential quiet stop receipts took about 95 ms before and 350-490 ms after, because each receipt now absorbs the recovery (local rehash, new submission and polls) that a periodic lookup previously absorbed.",
      "Mixed cohort: proof polls per lifecycle 13.5 before and 10.9 after; the quiet follower still lost its retained result to eviction once per run.",
      "Live cohorts are unchanged within run-to-run variation.",
      "All receipts verified, no transient retries, no dropped telemetry events."
